<article class="env-corollary" id="873F">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/873F">Corollary <span data-tag="873F">2.1.2.2</span> <span class="named">(Joyal)</span>.</a>left fibration!and undercategories Let $\calC $ be an $\infty $-category and $p: K \rightarrow \calC $ an arbitrary diagram. Then the projection $\calC _{p/} \rightarrow \calC $ is a left fibration. In particular, $\calC _{p/}$ is itself an $\infty $-category. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Apply Proposition <a href="/tag/F390" data-tag="F390">2.1.2.1</a> in the case where $X = \calC $, $S = \ast $, $A = \emptyset $, $B = K$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>